---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { currentChapter } from "../../data/currentChapter";
import { withBase } from "../../utils/paths";
const { venture, education } = currentChapter;
---
<BaseLayout title="Adren.ai / AdrenLabs — Caleb Perez’s Product & AI Work" description="Caleb Perez’s contribution to Adren.ai with the AdrenLabs founding team: product definition, agent workflows, technical prototyping and business research.">
<article class="case-page"><div class="shell">
  <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/#proyectos')}>← All ventures & projects</a>
  <header class="case-header"><p class="eyebrow">Current venture / {venture.period}</p><h1>Adren.ai<br /><span class="serif">Building with AdrenLabs.</span></h1><p class="case-deck">{venture.summary}</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={venture.productUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit Adren.ai ↗</a><a class="button button-secondary" href={venture.companyUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit AdrenLabs ↗</a></div></header>
  <dl class="case-meta"><div><dt>My role</dt><dd>{venture.role}</dd></div><div><dt>Team</dt><dd>Three-person team</dd></div><div><dt>Status</dt><dd>{venture.status}</dd></div><div><dt>Context</dt><dd>TETR · First semester in India</dd></div></dl>
  <section class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Context</p><h2>Understand before automating.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Business problems often sit between conversations, disconnected tools and informal processes. The starting point for Adren.ai is to understand that context before deciding what software should do.</p><p>AdrenLabs is the venture we are building; Adren.ai is the product I am developing with the team. The direction connects AI-assisted discovery and operational diagnosis with concrete requirements, prototypes and implementation priorities.</p></div></section>
  <section style="margin-top:65px" aria-labelledby="contribution-title"><p class="eyebrow">02 / My contribution</p><h2 id="contribution-title" style="margin-top:16px">Where I spend my time.</h2><div class="case-grid">{venture.contributions.map(item => <article class="case-note"><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.detail}</p></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Product thinking</p><h2>A direction we can test.</h2></div><div><p class="muted">A conceptual workflow, not a live demonstration or a claim that every stage is complete.</p><ol class="case-flow">{venture.workflow.map((step,index) => <li><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3 style="font-size:1rem">{step.title}</h3><p class="small muted" style="margin-top:10px">{step.detail}</p></li>)}</ol></div></section>
  <section class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / Learning in practice</p><h2>A venture alongside my AI degree.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>I am pursuing the {education.degree} at {education.institution}, {education.cohort}. Working on Adren.ai during my first semester in India connects coursework with product decisions, technical trade-offs and collaboration.</p><p>I bring experience from Zalmar Travel, API integrations, self-hosted systems and AI-assisted development. The next steps are to continue validating the problem, refine the prototype and document evidence as the work progresses.</p><p class="small">This page describes my contribution and our development direction, not independently verified business results. Future milestones will be added when achieved.</p></div></section>
  <div class="case-next"><a href={withBase('/#current-chapter')}><span>Continue reading</span>My TETR chapter ↗</a><p class="small muted" style="text-align:right">Updated {currentChapter.updated}</p></div>
</div></article>
</BaseLayout>
